      "side": 1,
      "message": "This does not look like correct server behavior.\n\nSection 5.1 says\n\n   The value of \u0027partial success\u0027 MUST be TRUE if the authentication\n   request to which this is a response was successful.\n   \nand Section 7 says\n\n   The server MUST respond to this message with either\n   SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_FAILURE or with the following:\n\n      byte      SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_PK_OK\n\nMy interpretation is that sending a partial success would mean the authentication has completed successfully, which is not possible following a request without a signature. Instead, the sequence should be: request without signature, SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_PK_OK, request with signature, SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_FAILURE with partial success.",
      "revId": "a094c6e94c171892ee16ca9134a6ea03e5dfea5f",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c02483f_5e69e705",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 60078
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T06:24:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Section 7 is about \"publickey\" auth method.\n\nAccoding to this section, \"when the server does not support some algorithm\", it will reject client with SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_FAILURE or SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_PK_OK.\n\nBut according to Section 5.1, if there is a response message with \"authentications that can continue\", the client should \"continue the authentication dialog\" with the method in name-list.\n\nFor my scene, the SSH Server should auth by \"publickey\" and OTP code, so when the server has been authed by \"publickey\", it will tell the client continue auth with OTP(keyboard-interactive).",
      "parentUuid": "aa18bcb3_ebdab01e",
      "revId": "a094c6e94c171892ee16ca9134a6ea03e5dfea5f",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
